<interrogationes unitas="delineare_mandata">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I render a Mandata list to pixels without opening a window?
    <responsum symbolum="tabula_pixelorum_creare_nuda delineare_mandata imago_ex_tabula imago_png_scribere">tabula_pixelorum_creare_nuda(piscina,
      latitudo, altitudo) gives a window-free table (scale 1), then
      delineare_mandata(m, tabula, fons, ctx). imago_ex_tabula views the
      result as an Imago without copying (the packed pixels already lie
      in memory as R, G, B, A), ready for imago_png_scribere. The new
      table is zeroed, i.e. black with alpha 0, so paint a background
      rectangle first if the PNG should not be transparent.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I get pictures drawn for MANDATUM_IMAGO elements?
    <responsum symbolum="ImagoFons delineare_mandata mandata_imago">Mandata
      never carry pixels: mandata_imago stores a name in textus, and the
      ImagoFons callback you pass to delineare_mandata turns that name
      into a constans Imago* (pictor uses the projection's sigillum).
      A NIHIL fons or a NIHIL result skips the element. The picture is
      cropped to the element's fines, scaled by the group's integer
      scale, pixels with alpha 0 are skipped, and every other pixel is
      copied as is - no blending.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what colour does a ColorMandati turn into when rasterized?
    <responsum symbolum="color_ex_mandato thema_color thema_color_ex_indice_colorationis color_ex_pixelum">color_ex_mandato
      decides: COLOR_MANDATI_THEMA goes through thema_color, so
      thema_initiare must have run; COLOR_MANDATI_INDEX through
      thema_color_ex_indice_colorationis, so its value is a syntax
      colouring index (ColoratioIndex), not a raw palette slot;
      COLOR_MANDATI_RGBA (and any other genus) is the
      packed table pixel a &lt;&lt; 24 | b &lt;&lt; 16 | g &lt;&lt; 8 |
      r read by color_ex_pixelum - not a literal 0xRRGGBBAA.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can text and lines follow a group's clip, scale and line thickness?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_mandata tabula_pixelorum_pingere_chordam_fonte" via="lib/delineare_mandata.worklog.md">Not
      in this V1 rasterizer. Text is placed at the group's origin and
      scale but drawn at the font's native cell size by
      tabula_pixelorum_pingere_chordam_fonte, and it ignores the group's
      sectio clip. Lines are always one pixel thick (crassitudo is
      ignored) and use only their first two points. Rectangles, lines,
      polygons and images do honour the clip, and their geometry
      follows the scale.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can mandata have negative coordinates, for content panned off the left or top?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_mandata delineare_ponere_praecisionem" via="lib/delineare_mandata.worklog.md">Yes
      for the primitives: rectangles, lines and polygons that reach into
      negative space are clipped in signed arithmetic before the
      unsigned delineare calls (which would vanish or hang otherwise).
      One gap remains: a group with sectio whose clip box starts left of
      or above 0 hands that origin to delineare_ponere_praecisionem,
      which raises it to 0 without shrinking the box, so the clip comes
      out wider or taller than the group by the overhang.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I rasterize only some of the primitives in a Mandata list?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_mandata_selecta DelineareFiltrum">delineare_mandata_selecta
      with a DelineareFiltrum: return VERUM to paint an element. The
      filter judges primitives only; groups are always walked, so
      transforms and clips stay exact for whatever you keep. A NIHIL
      filter paints everything, the same as delineare_mandata.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I nest groups (coetus) as deeply as I like?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_mandata mandata_coetus_incipere">Up
      to 63 levels below the root (the frame stack is LXIV). A deeper
      group is not pushed, without any warning: its contents are drawn
      in the enclosing group's origin, scale and clip, while the
      element counting still pops the outer frames
      correctly.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I rasterize the same Mandata every frame without its piscina growing?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_mandata delineare_creare_contextum mandata_vacare piscina_notare piscina_reficere">Not
      for free: every call allocates a ContextusDelineandi from the
      Mandata's own piscina (m-&gt;piscina), and every polygon three
      scratch arrays, none released. Rebuild the list per frame in a
      piscina you empty, or bracket the call with piscina_notare and
      piscina_reficere on that piscina.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what are delineare_mandata_modulus and delineare_mandata_mensor for?
    <responsum symbolum="delineare_mandata_modulus delineare_mandata_mensor modulus_creare">They
      declare this rasterizer's native scope for tessellation: the
      Modulus has the window's text cell as its cell and the table as
      its extent, and the ModulusMensor says text is measured by the
      font, one cell per rune (fons_6x8), grapheme policy. Text this
      rasterizer paints stays inside what that module
      measures.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
